======================================================================
RESTRICTION RANKING (fewer = better)
======================================================================

The SHARPEST mapping = the one where the realizable set is
the SMALLEST fraction of the total possible states.

From the data:
  1. SCC PARTITION: only 2 values at each n ({(1,1,...,1), (n,)}).
     This is the #SCC ∈ {1,m} result (HYP-2000). MOST restricted.
     BUT: too coarse — doesn't distinguish classes within each SCC type.

  2. SCORE SEQUENCE: much fewer than iso classes.
     Captures the 'shape' without the 'wiring'. Good balance.

  3. ISO CLASS: the baseline (A000568).

  4. GAP MULTISET: captures the geometric structure directly.
     The lonely gap multisets might be very restricted.

THE IDEAL: a mapping between SCC partition (too coarse) and
iso class (too fine) that captures exactly the LRC-relevant structure.
The SCORE SEQUENCE is the natural candidate.

